Originally, the debian/ folders for building Debian packages were included in the individual directories.
In order to make this cleaner for future package building and to comply better with Debian policies, the debian/ folders
have been moved into the root directory under debian-files/.

Each section has its own directory, and in there you will find debian/ and debian-original/.

debian-original/ is the original Debian package files provided with KDE1. These are used as reference for the modern version
that you will find under debian/.

To use them, simply copy the correct debian/ folder into the correct directory. Example for base:

cp -r debian-files/base/debian base/

**Building the meta-package(s)**

A meta package is a package that generally depends on other packages but does not install anything itself.
This is useful for providing one package to install a whole desktop environment made up of many packages, for example.

In MiDesktop, that package is midesktop-full.

To build this package:

```
cp -r debian-files/midesktop-full .

dpkg-deb --build midesktop-full

mv midesktop-full.deb midesktop-full_1.2.0~beta1_all.deb
```

Make sure to change the version section appropriately  so it matches the correct version of your install.
